From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 15:12:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: qca8k: configure QCA8386 2500BASE-X CPU pad

The QCA8386 CPU link uses SGMII+ on the switch side and fixed
2500BASE-X on the IPQ UNIPHY side. qca8k advertises the mode for
QCA8386, but qca8k_phylink_mac_config() returns before enabling the
port 0 SGMII pad when phylink selects 2500BASE-X. This leaves all user
ports with working PHY link state but no traffic through the CPU port.

Accept 2500BASE-X only for QCA8386 CPU port 0 and enable its SGMII pad.
The PPE/IPQ PCS remains responsible for configuring the 2.5G UNIPHY
side of the fixed link.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c
@@ -1446,7 +1446,9 @@ qca8k_phylink_mac_config(struct phylink_
 		    state->interface != PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_RGMII_ID &&
 		    state->interface != PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_RGMII_TXID &&
 		    state->interface != PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_RGMII_RXID &&
-		    state->interface != PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_SGMII)
+		    state->interface != PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_SGMII &&
+		    !(qca8k_is_qca8386(priv) &&
+		      state->interface == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_2500BASEX))
 			return;
 
 		reg = QCA8K_REG_PORT0_PAD_CTRL;
@@ -1502,6 +1504,7 @@ qca8k_phylink_mac_config(struct phylink_
 		break;
 	case PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_SGMII:
 	case PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_1000BASEX:
+	case PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_2500BASEX:
 		/* Enable SGMII on the port */
 		qca8k_write(priv, reg, QCA8K_PORT_PAD_SGMII_EN);
 		break;
